WEBVTT

00:09:58.912 --> 00:10:02.496
one of the things that I've long been
curious about when we see those kinds of

00:10:02.496 --> 00:10:06.746
differences, how much are they driven
by social roles versus, you know,

00:10:06.746 --> 00:10:11.204
more evolutionary and biologically rooted
forces? Where do you come down on that?

00:10:11.829 --> 00:10:14.996
Well, I think it's mostly I don't know.

00:10:14.996 --> 00:10:18.204
I mean, we do know now this
chimpanzee culture,

00:10:18.204 --> 00:10:23.537
a different chimpanzee communities have
slightly different ways of doing things.

00:10:23.829 --> 00:10:29.246
But that's mostly we see it in things
like tool using and sometimes using

00:10:29.454 --> 00:10:33.496
a gesture that's common to both. But
in a slightly different context.